  "latestMilestone": "Canonical SWIR_OS main now includes the verified native GTK4 Screenshot Tool source and security contract. Production capture requests org.freedesktop.portal.Screenshot on the authenticated user session bus with interactive consent/selection, accepts only bounded canonical local file results, rejects remote and symlink-traversing inputs, and writes an owner-only atomic local copy without shell capture, compositor-specific capture binaries, sudo or pkexec. Its dedicated policy, controlled session-D-Bus portal, real Weston/Wayland and Debian 13 target gates passed on the PR and again on canonical main. Graphical-image staging and SWIR shell launcher integration are explicitly still pending, so the authoritative roadmap intentionally remains 55/65 (84.6%). Physical Live USB qualification remains pending; Secure Boot and legacy BIOS are not claimed.",
